      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive log retention and disposal specification developed for our enterprise environment, aligned with NIST SP 800-92 guidance on computer security log management. Our infrastructure spans three tiers \u2014 local system-level logging on endpoints and servers, a mid-tier aggregation layer using our Splunk forwarders, and a centralized SIEM at the enterprise level \u2014 so the spec must address retention durations, storage capacity planning, and disposal procedures independently for each tier. For retention periods, reference the NARA General Records Schedule 20 as the baseline for federal records obligations and layer on any additional operational needs such as keeping firewall and IDS logs for at least three years and authentication logs for at least six years. The specification should also define how unneeded log data is securely disposed of at each tier, including cryptographic erasure or certified deletion methods where appropriate. Storage capacity estimates should account for peak logging volumes, particularly for sources like intrusion detection systems that may suppress individual events until activity thresholds are met, as well as sources that log every occurrence. Include guidance on which log types are configurable for event-level granularity versus those that aggregate before recording, and ensure the policy accounts for both. Please have a draft ready for review by the compliance team before our next quarterly audit cycle.",
